cit ucid="JP-1241203-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>1241203</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-2265302-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>2265302</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="US-4538150-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country> <doc-number>4538150</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1083680A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAKUSAKI KEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAKUSAKI, KEIJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAKUSAKI KEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAKUSAKI, KEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A radio receiver circuit (104) and a radio receiver circuit (105) receive a radio communication signal from a mobile station (109) and a calibration signal from a CDMA radio signal transmitter (110) for CAL through their respective receiving antennas (102, 103), and downconvert the received signals. A processor B (107) for CDMA signals (for CAL) monitors the downconverted calibration signals to measure characteristic errors of the receiver circuits and stores the measured characteristic errors in a correction table of record means (109). At the same time that the CDMA signal processor B (107) begins monitoring, a processor A (106) for CDMA signals (for communication) demodulates the downconverted CDMA communication signal from the mobile station (109) based on the characteristic errors stored in the correction table.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur des circuits (104 et 105) d'un récepteur radio qui reçoivent un signal de communication radio d'une station mobile (109) et un signal d'étalonnage d'un émetteur (110) de signaux radio AMRC pour CAL par leurs antennes (102, 103) réceptrices respectives et transposent par abaissement de fréquence les signaux reçus. Un processeur B (107) de signaux AMRC (pour CAL) contrôle les signaux étalonnés transposés par abaissement de fréquence afin de mesurer les erreurs caractéristiques des circuits du récepteur et enregistre les erreurs mesurées dans une table de correction d'un dispositif d'enregistrement (108). Au moment où le processeur B (107) de signaux AMRC commence son contrôle, un processeur A (106) de signaux AMRC (pour communication) démodule le signal de communication AMRC converti par abaissement de fréquence et provenant de la station mobile (109) sur la base des erreurs caractéristiques stockées dans la table de correction.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>